It's about how most software does insert quotes.  If you
have a line with nothing but two dashes, most software
sees that as a flag that your signature has started and
it does not quote from there on.  Since sigs are supposed
to be trimmed out of replies, this is a convenience to
the people who use software that does this.  BTW, it is
a requirement for good software to do this since it is a
standard rule.  It's a way of telling whether your posting
software is good quality of not.  I post from Google and
it is poor quality software.

